<title>VIETNAM: Vietnam sells 50 bln dong T-notes, rate 12.0 pct.</title>
<headline>Vietnam sells 50 bln dong T-notes, rate 12.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HANOI 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vietnam sold 50 billion dong ($4.29 million) worth of one-year Treasury notes with an annual coupon of 12.0 percent to domestic and foreign institutions at an auction on Wednesday, an official at the State Bank of Vietnam said.</p>
<p>The rate was unchanged from the last auction of government paper, on May 7, when the central bank issued 50 billion dong worth of one-year notes.</p>
